  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Hapur?", answer: "Write in with your child's programme, the subject that needs work, their current level and which exam session they are sitting, and a shortlist follows built entirely around that syllabus rather than around who lives nearby, since nobody teaching the IB is based inside the district. We fit the timing to your household before anything else gets discussed, a free trial happens before any commitment, and a different tutor gets suggested at once if the first match is not quite right." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE tutors in Hapur?", answer: "We do, working to Cambridge or Edexcel specifications and taught entirely over video rather than at your address, since Hapur district has no confirmed IGCSE school of its own. A request for Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, to take two frequent examples, gets matched by that exact code and tier, and lessons draw on the board's genuine past papers throughout." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Hapur?", answer: "They do not. Home visits from a tutor exist only in Gurugram and select parts of Delhi NCR, nowhere else, which means a Hapur lesson always happens live on video, one to one, with a shared screen standing in for a shared table. It is real, personal online tuition rather than any kind of promise that somebody will show up at your gate." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Hapur cost?", answer: "What you pay depends mostly on how scarce that exact subject and level are among tutors nationally, alongside session length and how recently the tutor last taught it, and we confirm your own number before the trial starts. Expect IB Diploma HL subjects to sit above Cambridge Core-level rates as a rule. Video delivery keeps travel out of the fee entirely, and families can pause or stop at any point without being tied into anything longer." },
    { question: "Which schools in Hapur offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None currently. Kendriya Vidyalaya at Babugarh Cantt, Delhi Public School Hapur and Dewan Public School are the city's best-known private options, and all three run CBSE; most other district schools sit on the UP Board. Families wanting IB or IGCSE locally day-board to schools in Ghaziabad, Noida or Meerut, or board a child further away." },
    { question: "My child studies IB or IGCSE at a school outside Hapur while we live here. Can a tutor help?", answer: "This describes most of our Hapur families, since the district itself teaches neither curriculum. We look at exactly what your child's own school in Ghaziabad, Noida or elsewhere is covering, right down to the subject and level, and build sessions around whatever the day looks like, whether that means an evening after a commute home or a stretch during a boarding-school holiday." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "There is, on every single match. Your child sits down with the tutor over video and works through something genuinely current from their coursework, free of charge and with no obligation attached. A short plan for the first month follows the trial, and from there you can go ahead, ask for adjustments, or simply try a different tutor instead." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a child in Hapur?", answer: "Yes, though only by guiding, never writing. That means helping choose a workable research question, explaining what each assessment criterion actually rewards, planning data collection, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting assessed work breaks IB academic integrity rules, so IB Gram tutors decline those requests." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Hapur family?", answer: "Tutors are matched across every major IB Diploma subject group relevant to a Hapur student, most often Maths Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Hapur, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, tutoring covers the full IB continuum for Hapur households whose child attends a school elsewhere or is moving between curricula. MYP work focuses on criterion-based analysis across sciences and languages and on the Personal Project process journal; PYP work covers reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research skills." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for IB or IGCSE students in Hapur?", answer: "It works well, particularly given how few local specialists exist for HL subjects or specific Cambridge codes, and given that no local IB or IGCSE school exists at all. A shared screen, marked-up past papers and recorded worked solutions cover nearly everything a tutor sitting beside your child would otherwise do, while opening the choice to specialists right across India." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Hapur students?", answer: "Every tutor is checked on qualifications, recent teaching experience with the exact subject and level, and their approach to assessment criteria before being introduced to a family. Given the lack of a local IB or IGCSE school in Hapur district, we look specifically for tutors who have taught that syllabus recently rather than a generalist. The free trial class then lets you judge fit for yourself." },
    { question: "When should my child in Hapur start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Starting at the course's opening, Class 11 for the IB Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge IGCSE, leaves time to fix foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all land. Families starting in the final year can still make genuine progress, with tutoring concentrated on the highest-value topics and past papers ahead of the exam series." },
    { question: "My child is switching from UP Board or CBSE to IGCSE. Can a tutor help?", answer: "Yes, and it is a common request from Hapur families moving a child toward a Cambridge or Edexcel school elsewhere around Grade 9. The real gap is usually question style rather than content: command words such as 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, ideally starting the term before the switch happens." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Hapur?", answer: "Yes, most Hapur households book weekday evening slots after a commute or school day, along with weekend mornings. Scheduling accounts for the district's summer heat, when families often prefer earlier evenings, and for the Garhmukteshwar mela period, when local roads and routines shift noticeably. Adding a second weekly slot ahead of mocks or an exam series is straightforward online." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Hapur?", answer: "Say so and we find someone else. Progress is reviewed with families every few weeks, with a re-match whenever the fit is wrong, rather than expecting a child to persist with a tutor who is not working. There is no long contract, so pausing or stopping sessions carries no penalty either." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Hapur school or with the IB or Cambridge boards?", answer: "No. IB Gram runs as an independent tutoring platform, with no affiliation to, endorsement from, or representation of any Hapur school, the schools named in nearby cities on this page, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. School names describe where Hapur families actually study, and tutors work to each school's own calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

